eached and  passed a thousand subscribers and a  hundred thousand views on my videos now  I know that isn't that much in the sort  of YouTube scheme of things like one of  my favorite channels Freddy W I think  they hit 1 million subscribers in their  first year but when I've realized when  I've thought about the fact that  you know I'm making videos about high  school maths and technology rather than  like viral videos about action or  explosions or comedy I think it's pretty  amazing that anyone who's subscribed at  all now even though I started this  channel to help others I want to share  with you a big lesson that I've learned  myself over the past year because of  this channel and basically that is if  you want to start something if you've  got an idea then the best thing you can  do like rather than start preparing and  arming and hiring is just get going give  it a shot it's gonna be pretty lousy to  start with and if you like me it might  stay Lau's you for a while but what  surprised me over and over again is the  fact that even though what I've been  doing is really simple and really basic  and there's lots of videos out there  which are much much better lots of  channels which really professional that  kind of thing it's still been really  helpful to people and that amazes me  like I'm not a super experienced teacher  this is I've been teaching you for six  years now and where I teach you know  there's quite frequently people who get  their certificates for 20 years of  service or 25 or whatever so I'm  surrounded by all these amazingly  skilled people I'm still learning a lot  myself and I'm just sort of a baby in  that way but the little contribution  that I've been on make is Verrill help  people and I think a lot of people out  there watching are able to do the same  thing you might not think of yourself as  much but if you get started give it a go  you might be really surprised by what  you're able to accomplish so I want to  say thank you to everyone out there for  joining me on this journey here's to  many more years and many more helpful  videos
 

